  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A pear-shaped hanging bladder of stitched membrane, eight centimetres tall, used above the branch for dried mat. It hangs from a single plaited loop, because a store touching the branch on two sides counts as a floor and belongs to the house rather than to the household, a distinction the smallfolk consider too obvious to state. The neck closure is a spiral of stiffened fibre that opens on a quarter turn and holds against the wind. It arrived crushed and is now supported internally; the closure still works.</p>",
